  "stage": "study-review",
  "summary": "I checked the complete expansive study for the 1962 First Sunday of Advent against its eleven bilingual appointments, the full-text authorization, the Missal and historical hand missal, and the cited exegesis. Both interpretations give the reader a distinct reason to await Christ and develop all four senses. Gregory I.1.3 and Chrysostom, Homily 24 on Romans 13:11, explain why the disciples can welcome the Judge and why the runner quickens near the prize even when a convert's zeal has cooled. Aquinas, Super Romanos 13, lectio 3 [86224], explicitly distinguishes Paul's comparison of believers' readiness from the Church's Advent use of their words in the person of those awaiting the Incarnation. Bellarmine on Psalm 84, O'Sullivan p. 259, supports the inference from the uncultivated flower to the Spirit and Mary, while Augustine on the same psalm, \u00a712, describes the furrow of confession and delight in giving. I also checked Ambrose X.41\u201345, Bede at Luke 21:32, Gu\u00e9ranger at the Communion on p. 137, and the appointed text boundaries. All 19 sealed file hashes matched. A fresh typesetting has 22 pages. This verdict covers the study source and its extent. Exact-PDF visual acceptance and the independent web review are separate judgments."
}
